# Copy this file to tools/.secrets/.env and fill in your values.
# tools/.secrets/ is gitignored — nothing here goes to GitHub.
#
# Run  node tools/doctor.mjs  to verify what's set up.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pick ONE of the three modes below.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Mode 1: Service-account key (works locally AND in CI). Recommended. ─────
#
# Set GOOGLE_SA_JSON to either an absolute path to the key file OR the raw
# JSON contents, and set both SHEET_IDs. Sheets/Drive must be shared with
# the SA email as Viewer.
#
# GOOGLE_SA_JSON=/Users/nnaugle/Code/called_to_serve/tools/.secrets/sa-key.json
# SUBMISSIONS_SHEET_ID=1zRulLylIJxaCL7jpH6DDzwsPyWoBdXwH8jaqQ3d8PWE
# ROSTER_SHEET_ID=1prR5rGLlYJjdLl2YwSlI7oIBSojUTeqyirE4CTNpHf4

# ── Mode 2: Application Default Credentials (no key file). Local only. ──────
#
# Install gcloud, run once:  gcloud auth application-default login
# Then set ONLY the SHEET_IDs (leave GOOGLE_SA_JSON unset):
#
# SUBMISSIONS_SHEET_ID=1zRulLylIJxaCL7jpH6DDzwsPyWoBdXwH8jaqQ3d8PWE
# ROSTER_SHEET_ID=1prR5rGLlYJjdLl2YwSlI7oIBSojUTeqyirE4CTNpHf4

# ── Mode 3: Published CSV (no auth at all). Privacy trade-off. ──────────────
#
# In each sheet: File → Share → Publish to web → CSV → copy the URL.
# Anyone with the URL can read the sheet, so this is best for the master
# roster (low sensitivity). Submissions have photos/bios — think twice.
#
# Photos still need auth (or making each photo "Anyone with link"), so this
# mode is most useful for text-only test runs of the parser.
#
# PUBLIC_SUBMISSIONS_CSV_URL=https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/e/.../pub?output=csv
# PUBLIC_ROSTER_CSV_URL=https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/e/.../pub?output=csv
